## Interface: 30300
## Title: Uncapped UI
## Notes: Modular, theme-aware UI toolkit shared by Uncapped addons.
## Author: Uncapped
## Version: 0.0.0
## SavedVariables: UncappedUIDB

UncappedNative.lua
# [#1008] Re-routes a leading-dot command onto a whisper-to-self while the player is
# a ghost, because the 3.3.5a client refuses to SEND a SAY while dead and SAY is what
# carries every dot-command on this realm. Loaded early and deliberately depends on
# nothing in this addon -- it only hooks SendChatMessage, and `.dropcombat` being
# reachable while dead should not rest on the UI toolkit having initialised.
UncappedCommand.lua
# [#1277] Shared view of server backpressure: the client half of AddonThrottle's
# "UTHR:<retryAfterMs>" notice. Loaded here, next to UncappedCommand.lua and for
# the same reason -- it is TRANSPORT, it depends on nothing in this addon (not
# even UncappedUIKit), and a panel being able to say "the server is busy" should
# not rest on the UI toolkit having initialised.
#
# It is in UncappedUI rather than in each addon that needs it because the state
# it tracks is per-CLIENT, not per-panel: one bucket, one retry-after window, one
# place that knows about it. Four separate bug reports were four features each
# failing to notice the same drop.
UncappedThrottle.lua
UncappedUI.lua
# Right after the namespace bootstrap: every other file may register a frame
# with it, and CreateWindow does so for free.
UncappedScale.lua
# Generated index of the background pattern library (Assets\Patterns).
# Only sets a table on the namespace, so it can load early.
Assets\PatternList.lua
Themes\ThemeManager.lua
Themes\DefaultTheme.lua
# ★ LOADED since 2026-09-04, and now the theme a player gets by
# default (see INITIAL_THEME_NAME in ThemeManager.lua). It sat unloaded for a
# month because every key in it was commented out "pending custom art" and it
# therefore deep-merged into an exact copy of Default -- /uitheme listed an
# "Uncapped" theme that reported success and changed nothing.
#
# It never needed the art. The look is stock Blizzard textures multiplied by a
# violet tint, which is why the dialog border keeps its relief and the corner
# gem just turns amethyst. `/uitheme default` returns the old stock look.
Themes\UncappedTheme.lua
# Must precede any control that can glow -- Controls\Button.lua calls
# AttachGlow from its skin function, which runs the moment a button is built.
# Geometry helper shared by every decorative layer (glow, rims, vignettes).
# Must precede them all.
Effects\NineSlice.lua
Effects\Glow.lua
# Depends on NineSlice only for load order tidiness; it builds plain textures.
